{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774300444,"nonce":"5pLe5C7ev1WOosOoV/9+F1RFgiI=","title":"Project registry: canonical name-to-path resolution via mandible CLI","message":"When agents need to find a project by name (e.g. \"feedbax\"), they currently guess paths or search the filesystem. This led to a concrete bug: filing git-bug issues in the wrong clone of a repo because the agent found /Users/mll/dev/feedbax before /Users/mll/Main/.../feedbax (the canonical clone with worktrees and develop branch).\n\n**Two complementary solutions:**\n\n### Solution A: Priority directory convention\nA configured \"mono repo root\" directory (e.g. ~/Main) that is always searched first when resolving project names. If a project exists there, it takes precedence over any other location. Simple, stateless, covers the common case.\n\n### Solution B: Full project registry (preferred long-term)\n`mandible project` subcommand that tracks known projects:\n- `mandible project register \u003cname\u003e \u003cpath\u003e` — register a project\n- `mandible project resolve \u003cname\u003e` — return canonical path for a project name\n- `mandible project list` — list all registered projects\n- Auto-discovery: scan configured directories on first run\n- Fuzzy matching for typos (\"feedbx\" → \"feedbax\")\n- Store in Mandible database alongside sessions/auth\n\n**Use case:** Before any agent operation that targets a repo by name (filing issues, creating worktrees, reading CLAUDE.md), the first step would be `mandible project resolve \u003cname\u003e` to get the canonical path. This eliminates the class of bugs where agents operate on the wrong clone/fork.\n\nRelated: issue 2404c03 (project-aware git-bug wrapper) would benefit from this registry as its resolution backend.","files":null}]}